  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.2. Increased capacity of member States to formulate and implement policies and strategies for creating decent work in the rural economy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In October 2021, the Government of Suriname approved the 5-year Development Plan 2022-2026 (Ontwikkelingplan)  elaborated under the lead of the Suriname Planning Office (SPS). The document includes analysis and strategic recommendations reflecting the aim to achieve Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), including SDG 8 on growth and decent work, while focusing on most impactful interventions allowing the country to exit the COVID-19 crisis. It is based on information, data, and analysis guiding the determination of the best way to achieve the objectives. For each policy area the analysis includes production and international trends, scenario definition and strategic interventions reflecting the immediate, short-term (2024) and medium term (2026). The policy areas relate to rural sectors and include forestry, agricultural production, fisheries, gold, onshore oil, transport, roads and dewatering, and spatial planning, among others. All of these sectors are part of, or directly linked to, the rural economy. The related strategies have been defined on the basis of enhanced knowledge and data and include innovative elements to address country-specific future of work, educational, demographic and technological challenges. Its implementation involves collaboration among various Government Ministries. Between January 2020 and November 2021, the ILO provided policy advice underpinning the policy making process in Suriname. This included technical support to the Suriname Planning Office (SPS) and the National Statistical Office to develop a new macroeconomic modelling tool. The ILO also undertook policy analysis on the basis of the results of the model with a view to policy development. Specific focus was given to  to developing interventions targeting the rural economy and the promotion of decent work in the agro-food and other rural economy sectors, which were designed and included in the development plan as direct application of model findings.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">3.2.1. Number of member States with measures for decent work in rural areas</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
